{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "NUM",
  "chapter": 23,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balaam said to Balak, Build me here seven altars, and prepare me here seven oxen and seven rams.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak did as Balaam had spoken; and Balak and Balaam offered on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altar a bullock and a ram.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balaam said to Balak, Stand by thy burnt-offering, and I will go: it may be the LORD will come to meet me: and whatever he showeth me I will tell thee. And he went to a high place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God met Balaam: and he said to him, I have prepared seven altars, and I have offered upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altar a bullock and a ram.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD put a word in Balaam's mouth, and said, Return to Balak, and thus thou shalt speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he returned to him and lo, he stood by his burnt-sacrifice, he, and all the princes of Moab.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took up his parable, and said, Balak the king of Moab hath brought me from Aram, out of the mountains of the east, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Come, curse Jacob for me, and come, defy Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How shall I curse, whom God hath not cursed? or how shall I defy, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD hath not defied?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For from the top of the rocks I see him, and from the hills I behold him: lo, the people shall dwell alone, and shall not be reckoned among the nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who can count the dust of Jacob, and the number of the fourth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "part",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Israel? Let me die the death of the righteous, and let my last end be like his!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak said to Balaam, What hast thou done to me? I took thee to curse my enemies, and behold, thou hast blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altogether.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he answered and said, Must I not take heed to speak that which the LORD hath put in my mouth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak said to him, Come, I pray thee, with me to another place, from whence thou mayest see them: thou shalt see but the utmost part of them, and shalt not see them all: and from thence curse them for me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he brought him into the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah, and built seven altars, and offered a bullock and a ram on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to Balak, Stand here by thy burnt-offering, while I meet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the LORD",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yonder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD met Balaam, and put a word in his mouth, and said, Go again to Balak, and say thus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he came to him, behold, he stood by his burnt-offering, and the princes of Moab with him. And Balak said to him, What hath the LORD spoken?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took up his parable, and said, Rise, Balak, and hear; hearken to me, thou son of Zippor:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent: hath he said, and shall he not do ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? or hath he spoke, and shall he not make it good?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I have received ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "commandment",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to bless: and he hath blessed, and I cannot reverse it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob, neither hath he seen perverseness in Israel; the LORD his God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him, and the shout of a king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God brought them out of Egypt; he hath as it were the strength of a unicorn.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no enchantment against Jacob, neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " any divination against Israel: according to this time it shall be said of Jacob and of Israel, What hath God wrought!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, the people shall rise up as a great lion, and lift up himself as a young lion: he shall not lie down until he shall eat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the prey, and drink the blood of the slain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak said to Balaam, Neither curse them at all, nor bless them at all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Balaam answered and said to Balak, Did I not tell thee, saying, All that the LORD speaketh, that I must do?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak said to Balaam, Come, I pray thee, I will bring thee to another place; perhaps it will please God that thou mayest from thence curse them for me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak brought Balaam to the top of Peor, that looketh towards Jeshimon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balaam said to Balak, Build me here seven altars, and prepare me here seven bullocks and seven rams.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NUM.23.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NUM.23.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Balak did as Balaam had said, and offered a bullock and a ram on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
